2 CONT =Children with Kerstin Bengtsdotter''' (Lilja av Värnäs)=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Christiern Olofsson Drake,''' Married to Ingeborg.
2 CONT * '''Ingeborg Olofsdotter,''' married before 1532 with the gunman Nils Arvidsson ( spar over star ).
2 CONT * '''Jöns Olofsson Drake,'''
2 CONT * '''Erik Olofsson Drake,'''
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children with '''Märta Arvidsdotter''' (Sparre över stjärna)=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Arvid Olofsson Drake,''' Died about 1535. Joined. Cavalry captain. Married 1: o 1533 to Brita Eriksdotter . Married 2: o with Brita Persdotter (Hård af Segerstad) , daughter of the gunner Peder Hård and Carin Tordsdotter ( St
2 CONC ore ).
2 CONT * '''Margareta Olofsdotter Drake,''' married after 1532 with the chief white man Lars Bröms to Borrarp
2 CONT * '''Claes Olofsson Drake,''' married before 1532-06-24 with Gunnhild Persdotter (Hård af Segerstad) , daughter of the gunner Peder Hård and Carin Tordsdotter ( Store ). 
2 CONT * '''Jöran Olofsson Drake,'''
2 CONT * '''Olof Olofsson Drake,'''
2 CONT * '''Anna Olofsdotter Drake,'''
2 CONT * '''Cecilia Olofsdotter Dake,'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source''' Dragon from Västbo -  https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Drake_fr%C3%A5n_V%C3%A4stbo#TAB_2
2 CONT
2 CONT =Biography=
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Dragon, family, by Author Bengt Hildebrand.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Band 11 (1945), page 396.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dragon, family of salvation from Småland and Östergötland. Mainly in Småland, during the late Middle Ages two low-genus families appear, in the literature called Sunnerbo-Drakarna and Västbo - Drakarna . Among the former were bl. 
2 CONC a. Magnus Birgersson Drake (lived still in 1465, was d.1474) to Kalvnäs in Högsby sn (Kalm.), joined Stäkeborg in 1427, governor of Aspeland and Sevede 1448 (cf. Svea High Court Liber causarum 60, no. 6, National Archives), En'ann
2 CONC an branch owned from the end of the 13th century to the end of the 16th century Ugglebo in Ryssby sn (Kronob.). The genealogy of the genus, which was disputed already in a succession process 1475, is nowhere fully satisfactory inv
2 CONC estigated; its weapon was a dragon. It has been stated, but without binding evidence, that from this lineage might have descended from the nobility genus introduced in 1646 and then called Drake af Torp and Hamra (probably extinct
2 CONC  in 1709); however, the christian name used in the later genus Christer suggests, however, friendship with Västboätten. The family included Colonel Johan Christersson Drake af Torp and Hamra, who fell in the battle of Landskrona i
2 CONC n 1677. Among his children are the chief lieutenant, Fredrik Drake (b. 1660), who fell in the battle of Pultava 1709 and is named in Heidenstam's novel "Poltava" in the "Carolines", and Sophia Drake (d. 1741 ), GM Lieutenant Colon
2 CONC el Jon Stålhammar and in the literature known as the one by Snoilsky in "Swedish pictures" sung "Woman at Salshult". - Västbo-Drakarnas (weapon: flying dragon) ancestor Kristiern Drake is said to have married Margareta Krumme, wid
2 CONC ow of the county governor Olof Jönsson (older Capricorn). The son Olof (Kristersson) Drake was a long time and still 1518 governor of Västbo. His daughter's son in the rider champion Olof Nilsson Drake (d. 1590) - on the ancestor 
2 CONC of the genus (weapon: spar over star) s that still survives in. the gracious lineage Stenbock - adopted the name D., and the genus introduced in 1625 and extinct in 1635, is known as Drake af Intorp . About Olof Nilsson's father's
2 CONC  cousin, the Swedish National Council, Arvid Knutsson ;, (d. 1497), and his son the gunman and the chief of governors, Olof Arvidsson (d. 1508), who took up the mother's weapon (capricorn), see Stenbock. Olof Kristersson D's son (
2 CONC Olof Nilsson D's uncle) Arvid Olofsson Drake (d. After 1532), joined in Allbo and Östbo, was the father of Märta Arvidsdotter, about 1550 m. Field Colonel Knut Håkansson (Hand); cf. Hand , family. Their son the governor Arvid Knut
2 CONC sson Drake (d. Trol. 1618) took the mother's name and became the ancestor of the family Drake af Hagelsrum, see this one.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sources''' Sources: Parchment Letter, RA; KH Karlssons and C »Annerstedts above under Art. Drake, medieval salvation family from Dalarna and Västmanlandj cited works. - Arvid Trolle's land book 1498 '..., published by JA Almqui
2 CONC st (Hist. Handl., 31, 1938); King Erik XIV's Judgment Book, published by C. Silfverstolpe (Hist. Acts, 13: 1, 1884), p. 53. - JA Almquist, The Civil Service in Sweden 1523-1630, 4 (1922-23) ; JE Almquist, Streamed contributions to
2 CONC . the history of family law (1932), p. 37 f .; G. Djurklou, About Göran Månssons to Bolmsnäs land book (HA Acts, 28: 1, 1885); dens., [Rec. by] The scholarly letter bestowed on ... the Swedish nobleman's genus ... by B. Schlegel &
2 CONC  C; A. Klingspor (Hist. Bibi., 3, 1877), p. IX; F. Drake, Tribal tables above adl. the eaters Hand and Drake af Hagelsrum (1898); G. The Elgen Paths, The introduced genealogy of the Swedish nobility, 2 (1926), pp. 290, 308; KH Kar
2 CONC lsson, Knut Håkansson Hands and his wife Märta Arvidsdotter Drake's family (Personhist. Journal, 3, 1901, tr. 1902); PG Vejde, Kronoberg County manor houses (Hyltén-Cavalliusfören's yearbook, 1928–29), p. 340 f. - About Sophia Dra
2 CONC ke, married Stålhammar, see Ellen Fries, Drawings from Swedish 'noble family life in old times, 1 (2: and ed., 1909).
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sbl/Mobil/Artikel/17618 Dragon, Relatives, by Swedish Biographical Dictionary]
2 CONT
2 CONT Drake, savior families from Småland and Östergötland. Mainly in Småland appear during the late Middle Ages two low-saved families, in the literature called Sunnerbo-Drakarna and Västbo - Drakarna . The former included a. Magnus Bi
2 CONC rgersson Drake(still living 1465, was d. 1474) to Kalvnäs in Högsby sn (Kalm.), bailiff at Stäkeborg 1427, district chief in Aspeland and Sevede 1448 (cf. Svea Court of Appeal Liber causarum 60, no. 6, National Archives), Another 
2 CONC branch owned from the end of the 14th century to into the 16th century Ugglebo in Ryssby sn (Kronob.). The genealogy of the family, which was already disputed in an inheritance process in 1475, is nowhere fully satisfactorily inve
2 CONC stigated; its weapon was a dragon. It has been stated, but without binding evidence, that from this family would possibly descend the noble family, which was introduced in 1646 and then became called Drake af Torp and Hamra (proba
2 CONC bly extinct in 1709); the baptismal name Christer used in the latter generation, however, rather indicates kinship with Västboätten. Colonel Johan Christersson Drake af Torp and Hamra belonged to the family, who fell in the battle
2 CONC  of Landskrona in 1677. His children include the lieutenant colonel, Fredrik Drake (b. 1660), who fell in the battle of Pultava in 1709 and is mentioned in Heidenstam's short story »Poltava» in »Karolinerna», and Sophia Drake (d. 
2 CONC 1741 ), gm Lieutenant Colonel Jon Stålhammar and in literature known as the one sung by Snoilsky in »Svenska bilder» «Frun på Salshult». - Västbo-Drakarnas (weapon: flying dragon) ancestor Kristiern Drake is said to have married M
2 CONC argareta Krumme, widow of the district chief Olof Jönsson (older Stenbocksätten). The son Olof (Kristersson) Drake was for a long time and still in 1518 district chief in Västbo. His grandson in the equestrian master Olof Nilsson 
2 CONC Drake (d. 1590) - on the father of the family (coat of arms: chevron over star) s that still survives in. the noble family Stenbock - took the name D., and the family branch introduced 1625 and extinct 1635, is known as Drake af I
2 CONC ntorp . About Olof Nilsson's father's cousin ,, Councilor Arvid Knutsson ;, (d. 1497) and his son the gunsmith and district chief Olof Arvidsson (d. 1508), who took up the maiden weapon (Capricorn), see Capricorn. Olof Kristersson
2 CONC  D: son (Olof Nilsson D: uncle) Arvid Olofsson Drake (d. After 1532), bailiff in Allbo and östbo, was the father of Märta Arvidsdotter, b. Around 1550 m. Field Colonel Knut Håkansson (Hand); cf. Hand , relatives. Their son the gov
2 CONC ernor Arvid Knutsson Drake (d. Trol. 1618) took the mother's name and became the ancestor of the family Drake af Hagelsrum, see this.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bengt Hildebrand.
