1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Christiern Drake af Västbo=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Kristiern is said to have had Danish origins and was the castle law at Alvsborg, before he settled in Sunnerbo, Bolmsö parish's then mainland and Västbo district, which after his death in 1484 should also have been Margareta Kru
2 CONC mme's widow's estate. In the genealogical literature, the genus is known as Västbodrakarna. 
2 CONT * Kristiern had only one son: Olof Kristiernsson Drake, who was probably born in the 1460s and died in 1518. He was married twice. In the first marriage to Kerstin Bengsdotter (lily of Värnäs), son 1. Kristiern Olofsson Drake was 
2 CONC born, whose son Birger Kristiersson signed Drake to Ramnäs. He had an illegitimate son Jöns, rider and father of Lieutenant Krister Drake, who was knighted to Drake by Torp and Hamra. 2. Ingeborg Olofsdotter was Kristieren's siste
2 CONC r in Olof Kristiernsson's first marriage. She was married to Nils Arvidsson (Drake av Intorp) with descendants within the later generations of this family. No later than 1508, Olof Kristiernsson remarried to Märta Arvidsdotter (Dr
2 CONC ake av Intorp), daughter of the Riksrådet and the lawyer Arvid Knutsson (a cousin of Olof's brother-in-law Nils Arvidsson) and Anna Gustafsdotter (Stenbock ää, granddaughter of Margareta Krumme's first husband Olov Stenbock). With
2 CONC  this marriage, Olof became the brother-in-law of Olof Arvidsson, the ancestor of the younger Capricorn family. Several of Olof and Marta's children also had genealogically interesting descendants. Two of the sons, Arvid and Claës
2 CONC , each married sister Pedersdotter Hård of Segerstad. 3. Arvid Olofsson Drake was married to Brita Pedersdotter (Hård av Segerstad). In 1330 he acquired Ryd and Hammar (later Bolmsnäs> Liljenäs) in Torskinge, which the widow after
2 CONC  Arvid's death in 1335 brought with her in her new marriage to Jöran Jönsson (swan). married each sister Pedersdotter Hård of Segerstad. 3. Arvid Olofsson Drake was married to Brita Pedersdotter (Hård av Segerstad). In 1330 he acq
2 CONC uired Ryd and Hammar (later Bolmsnäs> Liljenäs) in Torskinge, which the widow after Arvid's death in 1335 brought with her in her new marriage to Jöran Jönsson (swan). married each sister Pedersdotter Hård of Segerstad. 3. Arvid O
2 CONC lofsson Drake was married to Brita Pedersdotter (Hård av Segerstad). In 1330 he acquired Ryd and Hammar (later Bolmsnäs> Liljenäs) in Torskinge, which the widow after Arvid's death in 1335 brought with her in her new marriage to J
2 CONC öran Jönsson (swan).
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Drake_fr%C3%A5n_V%C3%A4stbo#TAB_1 Dragon from Västbo, by Adelsvapen]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Christiern Drake''', död före 1484. Väpnare. Gift efter 1484Sic! ( efter 1456) married  '''Margareta Svensdotter (Krumme)''', dotter av Sven Bäk d.y. (Krumme) och Botild Klausdotter Abildgaard.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Olof Drake Häradshövding,'''  Gunman, district chief. Married 1st with Kerstin Bengtsdotter (Lilja av Värnäs) , daughter of Bengt Gjordsson ( Lilja av Värnäs ). Married 2nd before 1508 to Märta Arvidsdotter (chevron over star
2 CONC ), daughter of Arvid Knutsson Drake of Intorp No. 82 & Anna Göstafsdotter.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sbl/Presentation.aspx?id=17618 Dragon, Relatives, the Swedish Biographical Dictionary]
2 CONT
2 CONT Drake, savior families from Småland and Östergötland. Mainly in Småland appear during the late Middle Ages two low-saved families, in the literature called Sunnerbo-Drakarna and Västbo - Drakarna . The former included a. Magnus Bi
2 CONC rgersson Drake(still living 1465, was d. 1474) to Kalvnäs in Högsby sn (Kalm.), bailiff at Stäkeborg 1427, district chief in Aspeland and Sevede 1448 (cf. Svea Court of Appeal Liber causarum 60, no. 6, National Archives), Another 
2 CONC branch owned from the end of the 14th century to into the 16th century Ugglebo in Ryssby sn (Kronob.). The genealogy of the family, which was already disputed in an inheritance process in 1475, is nowhere fully satisfactorily inve
2 CONC stigated; its weapon was a dragon. It has been stated, but without binding evidence, that from this family would possibly descend the noble family, which was introduced in 1646 and then became called Drake af Torp and Hamra (proba
2 CONC bly extinct in 1709); the baptismal name Christer used in the latter generation, however, rather indicates kinship with Västboätten. Colonel Johan Christersson Drake af Torp and Hamra belonged to the family, who fell in the battle
2 CONC  of Landskrona in 1677. His children include the lieutenant colonel, Fredrik Drake (b. 1660), who fell in the battle of Pultava in 1709 and is mentioned in Heidenstam's short story »Poltava» in »Karolinerna», and Sophia Drake (d. 
2 CONC 1741 ), gm Lieutenant Colonel Jon Stålhammar and in literature known as the one sung by Snoilsky in »Svenska bilder» «Frun på Salshult». - Västbo-Drakarnas (weapon: flying dragon) ancestor Kristiern Drake is said to have married M
2 CONC argareta Krumme, widow of the district chief Olof Jönsson (older Stenbocksätten). The son Olof (Kristersson) Drake was for a long time and still in 1518 district chief in Västbo. His grandson in the equestrian master Olof Nilsson 
2 CONC Drake (d. 1590) - on the father of the family (coat of arms: chevron over star) s that still survives in. the noble family Stenbock - took the name D., and the family branch introduced 1625 and extinct 1635, is known as Drake af I
2 CONC ntorp . About Olof Nilsson's father's cousin ,, Councilor Arvid Knutsson ;, (d. 1497) and his son the gunsmith and district chief Olof Arvidsson (d. 1508), who took up the maiden weapon (Capricorn), see Capricorn. Olof Kristersson
2 CONC  D: son (Olof Nilsson D: uncle) Arvid Olofsson Drake (d. After 1532), bailiff in Allbo and östbo, was the father of Märta Arvidsdotter, b. Around 1550 m. Field Colonel Knut Håkansson (Hand); cf. Hand , relatives. Their son the gov
2 CONC ernor Arvid Knutsson Drake (d. Trol. 1618) took the mother's name and became the ancestor of the family Drake af Hagelsrum, see this. - https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sbl/Presentation.aspx?id=17619
2 CONT
2 CONT =Sources=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Dragon from Västbo on Adelsvapen-Wiki. Based on Gustaf Elgenstierna, The genealogy of the introduced Swedish nobility. 1925-36 ..
2 CONT * Jan Raneke, Swedish medieval weapons.
2 CONT * Jan Almquist The common ancestry of Drake's descendants. Family and tradition , 1957.
2 CONT * Drakeska genealogical archive, UB, and G. Drakes' above-mentioned typed genealogical chronicle; Correspondence between Archbishop Eric Benzelius the Younger and his brother ... Gustaf Benzelstierna, published by JH Liden (1791),
2 CONC  p. 104.
2 CONT * F. Drake, Stamtaflor öfver adl. the families Hand and Drake af Hagelsrum. (1898).
2 CONT * On many of the family's members see Nina Hammarskjöld, Ätten Hammarskjöld (1915), and Malin Mattsson, In Ydre in the 19th century (1932); om apotekaren Gustaf Drake (t 1939) se: T. Fredbärj, Gustaf Drake af Hagelsrum [Nekrolog o
2 CONC ch bibliografi] (Sv. Linné-älsk: s årsskr., 23, 1940), CFV Schimmelpfennig & K. Ahlberg, Sveriges apotekarhistoria, 5 (1936).
