1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Elin Jakobsdotter (Bååt)=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Elin Jakobsdotter Bååt is supposedly the daughter of Jakob Jacobson Snakenborg and Holmfrid Pedersdotter Pik.?  After further research, I’ve come across a source that shows Holmfried Pedersdotter Pik may not be the mother of Eli
2 CONC n Jakobsdotter Baat.  [https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=4579386&photo_id=6000000085090079897&position=1 '''From the Eskilsäter Church, Värmland Funeral Banner Family Board for Lennart Silfversvärd, shows 
2 CONC Holmfrid Pedersdotter Pik’s birth and death dates as 1660-1611?  Either these dates are incorrect or Holmfried Pedersdotter Pik isn’t Elin Jakobsdotter Baat’s mother.  Lennart Silfversvärd Family Banner shows Elin Jakobsdotter (Bå
2 CONC åt)  was born in 1578 and died in 1643, something is definitely wrong here.''']
2 CONT * Jakob Jonsson Til Làng 1540-1604 was Elin’s Stepfather.  Elin’s mother Married Jakob Jonsson, i Lång, Grums, in 1580, when Elin was around 2 years old. In a letter from Duke Carl, dated March 21, 1580, "our beloved Jakob Jonsson
2 CONC " is allowed to use the estates that he and his wife acquired from her father Pär Larsson "which are lying in Värmland", but with the condition that not on any way to dispose of them without first "offering and granting ourselves 
2 CONC to all others". This freedom from taxation has somehow been suspended temporarily and in a letter from Jakob Jonsson to Duke Carl, dated Gripsholm on April 23, 1595, he writes: "I, Jakob Jonsson to Lång, confess that after my K. W
2 CONC ife Hamfrid Pedersdotter, they have squandered her estate were inherited, under Cronan, for the reason that she took me as a married man as an unsalvated man, and Sweden's law contains that a freed woman farmer, then gives tax and
2 CONC  debt as a farmer..." after further attestations, "... with the good consent of my wife and relatives is given and given... His Princely Grace... my wife's inheritance Söderby named in Sone parish on Kållen in Västergötland lies..
2 CONC . to eternal property. . and for further confirmation I request the seals of the honest and virtuous men Nils Månsson and Olaf Cristoffersson as well as my own below this letter..." By this counterstroke it seems that he cleared u
2 CONC p the situation. Frälsegården Mellbyn in Bro (S) was owned in turn by Peder Larsson till Bro, Jakob Jonsson and Elin Jakobsdotter. Kjell Magnell - SoH 1965 no. 2-3 p.415-416. Frälsegården Mellbyn in Bro (S) was owned in turn by Pe
2 CONC der Larsson till Bro, Jakob Jonsson and Elin Jakobsdotter. Died around 1605 in Lång, Grums (S) [1] . Source: Kjell Magnell Family and Family 1965 p.397-420.
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id= 6000000085090079897&size=large}}
2 CONT
