2 CONT * Married: [https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000002842957594?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000191489347828 '''Lars Larsson den Aldre, Silfverswärd,'''] son of Lars Jonsson, (i Kvänum) and Margareta Hartmansdotter
2 CONT *  [https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000002842957594?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000191489587873 '''2nd: Source: Deeds of Sale Reduction Office,  (Volume) 126 from the National Archives of Sweden records the marriage o
2 CONC f Lars Larsson den Aldre, Silfverswärd & Karin Lennartsdotter Svenske.''']
2 CONT * Married: (2nd) in 1648 to [https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000002843141352&photo_id=6000000191488737834&position=2 '''Major Håkan Larsson, adlad Svärdsköld,'''] in his 2nd marriage, died 1654), die
2 CONC d 1678-01-00 and lies with both his men and the stepson Olov buried in Kvänum according to the inscription on their epitaph, then, daughter of the rider champion Lennart (Linder) Pedersson Svenske and Elin Bååt . 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Silfversw%C3%A4rd_nr_184 The Noble Family Silfverswärd No. 184]
2 CONT
2 CONT Lars Larssonthe older, adlad Silfverswärd, (son of Lars Jonsson, tab 1), to Badene, which he bought from the Crown 1642-08-30 and Vägestorp and Kvänum, which he received in donation, all in Kvänums parish, Skaraborg County. Was in
2 CONC cluded in the war service circa 1602 and served up from common to rider champion at Västgöta cavalry regiment. Also in charge of the district in Laske, 1624-10-22, which he was still in 1627. Major of the regiment in 1633. Adlad p
2 CONC . 20/10 (intro. 1633 under no. 184). Lieutenant Lieutenant at the same regiment in 1633. Slottshauptman at Älvsborg 1634-10-30. Farewell 1640-08-21. Equestrian at the nobility's rust service in Östergötland, Södermanland, Närke an
2 CONC d Värmland pp. 1/10. Died 1645-08-17 and buried in Kvänum's old, now ruined church. 'He was adored by King Gustaf II Adolf in the camp at Ribnitz in Mecklenburg, however, without any other noble name being allowed to him other tha
2 CONC n that the coat of arms painted on the original letter of honor is signed Larz Larzon Silberschwerdt '. Married 1st with (not known). Married 2nd: 1629, when she received Storebacka in Saleby parish, Skaraborg County in morning gi
2 CONC ft1 , with '''Karin Lydersdotter Svenske in her 1st marriage (married 2nd 1648 to Major Håkan Larsson, adlad Svärdsköld , in his 2nd marriage, died 1654), died 1678-01-00 and lies with both his men and the stepson Olov buried in K
2 CONC vänum according to the inscription on their epitaph, then, daughter of the rider champion Lennart (Linder) Pedersson Svenske and Elin Bååt .'''] According to Palmsköld's Genealogical Collections, Catharina Svenske had three sons w
2 CONC ith Silfverswärd, but in a Swedish family inheritance and payment settlement at the end of the 1600s only the following children Margareta, Agneta and Lars, as her inherited children are included. In March 1648, she was pardoned w
2 CONC ith three homemakers Vånga and Kvänum in the so-called Snr Skaraborg County '.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT *  '''Margareta,''' dead about 1682. Married 1st: with his step brother, driver Lars Svärdsköld , died in 1656. Married 2nd before 1660 with his sister's brother-in-law Lieutenant Göran Dreffensköld , died in 1672.
2 CONT *  '''Agneta,''' dead 1715-03-00 The path and buried s. Å 1/4. Married to Captain Carl Didron , natural. Didron , born 1630, died 1685.
2 CONT * '''Lars,''' the youngest. Cavalry captain. Died 1676. See Tab. 24
2 CONT * '''Maria,''' died in 1691 and buried s. On 4/7 in Gothenburg. Married before 1665 with the rider champion Björn Dreffensköld , died in 1684.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''source''' The noble family Silfverswärd No. 184, Tab 3 
2 CONT
