2 CONT 5) Called the old seat farm in 1681 and was then owned by the major Sv. Liedeman.
2 CONT
2 CONT 6) Now called Kristineberg. In 1681 it also bore the name of an old manor house. Owned then by wife Karin Svenske: 1683 by Ingehorg Silfversvärd. Yar Linnart Svinhufvud's estate in 1664. Bought from the provost Nils Hessel-gren in
2 CONC  1697 by the county chief J. Leijonbjelke for 510 r:dr curant, d. eh. 765 dalers silver coins. Built in 1805 by the provost L. Wallstedt; 1850 by commission surveyor H. Marin. m. fl.
2 CONT
2 CONT 7) Skrefs Dyngowiik 1449. Owned then by the squire Sven Jonsson, and thus an ancient manor. See a morning gift letter issued by him at Grinstad parish, No. 8. The same Sven Jonsson is mentioned in a letter on 10 February. 1494 (pr
2 CONC inted by Lilljegren after the original in v. Engeströmska library, 1819. page 41). published by Magnus Bonde's widow Kadrin Ingwarsdotter. Owned in 1563 by the well-to-do wife Karin, who owned both Dingelviks farms. Lästviken, Åse
2 CONC n, Högen, Hölgerud, Hafden, Bågen, etc. fl. In 1577, Nils Månsson at Bro was the owner of this: 1664 wife Margareta Svenske: 1783 court junior Reuter: 1809 horse master Sam. Tile: 1827 Carl Pet. Åberg: 1845 crown county in Näs dis
2 CONC trict of Wermland JF Wennerlöf: 18-17 baron St. Gyr and countess Ramel, born Lewenhaupt.
2 CONT
2 CONT 8) Has mostly had the same owner, as Norra Dingelvik. But owned in 1681 by Major Gregor. Ahlfclt, 1768 by the utility patron Sam. Chef.
2 CONT
2 CONT 9) Has also had the name Ekarebol. Called new manor in 1681. Owned then by Linnart Svinhufvud: 1783 by Sergeant Svinlmfvud: 1850 by C. Fr. Wow.
2 CONT
2 CONT 10) Old manor house. See X:o 7. Egdes 1664 by wife Margareta Svenske: 1686 by ensign Lars Svinhufvud: 1600 by Luiradshöfdingen Joh. Rho-din. who bought this manor from the latter for 500 riksdaler curant. 1 in later times belonged
2 CONC  to the owners of Billingsholm ironworks.
2 CONT
2 CONT 11) See i\:o 7. Was in 1664 well-born Patrik Tbomson's seat farm; 1681 Mrs. Agneta S\renskes: *Häradshöfdingcn. the assessor de Freses; In 1809 the commissioner was
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Sv%C3%A4rdsk%C3%B6ld_nr_334 Noble House Sword Shield No. 334]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Noble House Sword Shield No. 334, Knighted 1645-10-06, introd. 1647. Extinct in the early 18th century.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT In Schlegel & Klingspor, The unintroduced adelns ätartavlor, it is stated that the noble Håkan Larsson Svärdsköld was the brother of Lars Larsson, noble Silfverswärd, and Jon Larsson, progenitor of the noble families Svärdfelt. An
2 CONC y other source for this than the floating information in Fryxell, Vermland's genealogy book, that this would have been the case, is not cited, nor should there be any. In the mention in the knight house genealogy of Lars Silfversw
2 CONC ärd's widow Karin Svenske's remarriage to Håkan Larsson Svärdsköld, it is not implied that the two men were brothers, which would certainly have happened, if that had been or was considered to be the relationship. In addition, the
2 CONC  court's permission had to be obtained for Margareta Silfverswärd's marriage to her stepbrother Lars Svärdsköld, since the two parties were also cousins. but no such condition seems to have been invoked. Håkan 
2 CONT
2 CONT Håkan Larsson , knighted Sword Shield, to Vistaholm in Floby parish, which he received as a donation on 29-03-1649 under the terms of the Norrköping decision, and Nygården in Kvänum parish, which he received through his later marr
2 CONC iage, both in Skaraborg county. Horseman at the Västgöta Cavalry Regiment. Knighted 1645-10-06 (introd. 1647 under no. 311, which number has since been changed to 334). Major 1650. Died 1654-04-27 and is buried with his second wif
2 CONC e and her first husband in Kvänum's church. Married 1st to N . N. _ '''Married 2nd in 1648 to Karin Lennartsdotter Svenske in her 2nd marriage (married 1st in 1629 to lieutenant colonel Lars Larsson the elder, ennobled Silfverswär
2 CONC d , in his 2nd marriage, died 1645), died 1678-01-00, daughter by the master rider Lennart Svenske, and Elin Bååt.''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1. '''Lars''' Driver. Died 1656. Lars (son of Håkan Larsson, knighted Sword Shield, Tab. 1). Driver at Västgöta Cavalry Regiment. Died without sons in 1656 in the city of Holland (?) in Prussia. Married to his step-sister Margar
2 CONC eta Silfverswärd in her 1st marriage (married 2nd before 1660 to his sister's brother-in-law, lieutenant Göran Dreffensköld , died 1672), died about 1682, daughter of lieutenant-colonel Lars Larsson the elder, ennobled Silfverswär
2 CONC d , and his 2nd wife Carin Lennartsdotter Swedish . Children: Agneta , born 1655, died 1712-07-22 at Frändö in Färgelanda parish, Älvsborg county. Married before 1684 to Major Lars Fahnesköld , died around 1702.
2 CONT * 1. '''A son.''' Died during the war in Poland in the 1650s. [ 1 ]
2 CONT * 1. '''Goran''', to Vistaholm, which was reduced from him but exchanged in 1685, as well as Brandstorp in Hällestad parish, Älvsborg County, which he held for a time through his marriage. Traveled abroad in 1664 to study the mili
2 CONC tary and was for ten years one after the other in Dutch, French and Italian service and advanced to major. Still alive in 1700. Died childless and ended the family on the side of the sword. 'He was, during his foreign service, las
2 CONC t employed in the guard of the Grand Duke of Tuscany and in charge of the galleys at Malta. When the galley on which he served was shot down by a Turkish privateer, was captured. During the captivity, God made a promise, as a resu
2 CONC lt of which, after returning to his fatherland, both from the little he himself could save, and from the small donation that his father had acquired with his blood, built a church and bequeathed all his property to the poor and th
2 CONC e church service, although he requested confirmation in 1685. Then gave to the Crown £100 interest and what he could afterwards collect.'. Married in 1674 toMärta Krabbe af Svaneby , from whom he was divorced in 1693, in her 2nd m
2 CONC arriage (married 1st to the captain Carl Hård af Segerstad , died 1657), died 1699-02-00, daughter of lieutenant colonel Gustaf Krabbe af Svaneby , and his 1st wife Anna Carlsdotter Lilliestielke.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Links=
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://runeberg.org/anrep/4/0317.html
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Sources =
2 CONT
2 CONT * EÄ258, Till Säter samt Åttingsåker i Färgelanda sn (P) (1655). Fick Storebacka i Saleby sn (P) i morgongåva av Lars Silfverswärd.  Ligger jämte båda sina män och styvsonen Olov begr i Kvänum enligt påskriften å deras epitafium d
2 CONC ärst. "Catarina Svenske skulle enligt Palmskölds Genalogiska samlingar haft med Silfverswärd tre söner, men uti en Svenske-ättens arvs- och vederlagslikvid i slutet av 1600-talet upptages då endast de nedanstående barnen    Margar
2 CONC eta, Agneta och Lars, såsom hennes i arv delaktiga barn; hon blev 1648-03-20 benådad med tre hemman Vånga och Kvänum i likan.  snr (Skar)."                                                     
