1 NOTE http://home.c2i.net/cowe/mowat/hugoland.htm Elses 3. ektemann. Fra 'The
2 CONT Science of Planck_LFI' (Oslo University) 'To start at the beginning, we
2 CONT have to take a detour to 16t h century Scotland and Shetland. The
2 CONT northern Scottish isle s, Shetland and Orkney, had from the Viking age
2 CONT been closel y connected with Norway, the language was Norwegian (a Norw
2 CONT egian dialect, called Norn, was spoken in remote places unt il the 18th
2 CONT century) and they were ruled by the semi-indepe ndent Earl of Orkney as a
2 CONT fief under the King of Norway. Th e Earl of Orkney was the second highest
2 CONT ranking man in Norw ay, only the King ranked higher. Already in the 14th
2 CONT centur y some Scottish influence came to Orkney and Shetland. Whe n the
2 CONT last earl of Norwegian descent died in 1379, the earl dom was inherited
2 CONT by the Lowland Scottish noble family Sinc lair. The first Sinclair was a
2 CONT Norman knight, called de St . Clair, who had accompanied William the
2 CONT Conqueror to Engla nd in 1066. For the next century, the highest ranking
2 CONT Norwe gian after the King was a Scotsman. In 1471, the King of De
2 CONT nmark-Norway (Denmark and Norway were from 1397 united i n a union which
2 CONT lasted until 1814) gave the earldom of Orkn ey, including Shetland, to
2 CONT the king of Scotland as securit y for a loan which was used to pay the
2 CONT dowry when his daugh ter was married to the Scottish king. The loan was
2 CONT never pa id back, and Orkney and Shetland have since then been par t of
2 CONT Scotland. In the 16th century, a substantial immigration of Scotsme n to
2 CONT Orkney and Shetland started, and several Scottish nobl emen managed to
2 CONT acquire large estates on Shetland. One wh o most probably was among these
2 CONT immigrating Scottish noblem en was the one who later laid the first
2 CONT foundations for th e estates which would become Rosendal Barony in
2 CONT Norway, And rew Mowatt. The Mowatt family also descended from one of th e
2 CONT Norman knights who followed William the Conqueror, the fa mily name was
2 CONT originally de Montealt. The family had acquir ed a fief in Scotland early
2 CONT in the 12th century. In the 16t h century the main branch of the Mowatt
2 CONT family held the lor dship of Balquholly in Aberdeenshire. Andrew Mowatt
2 CONT was cle arly a close relative of the lord of Balquholly, but we d o not
2 CONT know who his father was, and exactly what this kinshi p was. However, we
2 CONT know that his mother was called Barbar a Sinclair, and that she was a
2 CONT descendant of the earlier ea rls of Orkney. The first mention of Andrew
2 CONT Mowatt in any kn own sources is from 1558. He was then clearly an adult,
2 CONT h e was married to Ursula Tulloch, and he was an estate owne r on
2 CONT Shetland, mentioned as the lord of Hugoland. Since n o Mowatts are found
2 CONT in earlier Shetland sources, Andrew mos t probably had come from Scotland
2 CONT as the first Mowatt on Sh etland some time before 1558. Besides his
2 CONT landed estates o n Shetland, which he transferred to his sons in 1577,
2 CONT Andre w Mowatt was also a businessman, owning a number of merchan t ships
2 CONT and doing trade with Norway, Scotland and England . His wife Ursula died
2 CONT some time in the 1580s, and in 158 7 he wrote an application to the King
2 CONT of Scotland to be all owed to travel to Bergen in Norway to get married.
2 CONT And shor tly after, he did travel to Bergen and there he married th e
2 CONT twice before widowed Else Rustung, daughter of Admiral o f the
2 CONT Danish-Norwegian Navy Christopher Trondsson Rustung , a most adventurous
2 CONT person.' Ifølge Danmarks Adels årbok, som har hentet sine opplysning er
2 CONT fra en gammel anetavle, så er det Bertil ( Bartholome w ) Mowat som var
2 CONT faren til Anders. Han ble ikke nevnt sene re, så mye kan tyde på at han
2 CONT døde i ung alder. Han bodde p å Balquholly i Banffshire i Skottland. Mye
2 CONT kan tyde på at d et er Bertil ( Bartholomew ) som er faren til Anders,
2 CONT ford i den eldste sønnen til Anders fra hans ekteskap med Ursul a Tolloch
2 CONT på Shetland fikk navnet Berald, som er en annen v ariant av navnet
2 CONT Bartholomew. Slekten Mowat i Skottland ko m fra Normandie i Frankrike på
2 CONT 1200-tallet, hvor det opprin nelige navnet var Monthaut ( De Montealt ).
