2 CONT * Born in Dalarna, Died in Norra Åsum/L in the war between Sweden and Denmark. Norra Åsum is located by Kristianstad. Major and District Chief	
2 CONT * Pig head in Westergötland, Rank: Noble Family number: 199, Knighted: 1581-06-22, Introduced: 1633-02-15 Origin: Sweden, Dalarna, Falun, Hästberg.
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/photo/view/4579755?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000190255554944 '''RIKSDAGSPROTOKOLL, page 151''']
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=4579755&photo_id=6000000116555784907&position=6 '''Värmlands regementes (Närkes och Värmlands regementes) historia, Volumes 1-2 By Carl Otto Nordensvan'''] 
2 CONT * February 15, 1633, Major Carl Jönsson introduced to Norra Dingelvik in Steneby parish, Älvsborgs län († 1636), Eight Svinhufvud in Westergötland at Riddarhuset. The eater was entered under the full name Svinhufvud in Westergötla
2 CONC nd, no. 199, in order to be easily distinguished from the 1620 introduced eater Svinhufvud (of Qvalstad), no. 145. (note Kerstin Melin)
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=4579755&photo_id=6000000194351930822&position=0 '''It is not very often that we see the family name printed in the early 17th century, but here is an example from the c
2 CONC ourt at Kopparberget 16 March 1619, where it appears that Karl Jönsson Svinhufvud had pledged Klubbtäkten to Kristoffer Olofsson (Gyllenknoster) in Noret for 10 skepunds of raw copper (Hela Dalarna tingslag district court (W) AI:1
2 CONC 1 (1618-1619) Image 1690 / page 472 (AID: v222742.b1690.s472, NAD: SE/ULA/10391)).''']
2 CONT * Of the noble wheat Svinhufvud in Västergötland. To Stora Dingelvik in Steneby, Lieutenant at Närkes and Värmlands regiment 1622, later in 1634.
2 CONT * Heardshövding in the town of Skärkind, Östergötland, 1635.
2 CONT * Died in Verben, Saxony, during the 30-year-old chick.
2 CONT * To Stora Dingevik in Stenby parish at Dal f about 1585 Introduced in 1633 as No. 199 Häradshövding, Major Got 1649 in donation six treasure troops in the Kingdom of Sweden, Småland. Living description Born 1602 in Eskilsäter/S. 
2 CONC died 1673 in Steneby/P. To your gel cove and pile, Steneby. Margareta was widowed 1636, when her husband died in the verbs, Saxony, during the 30-year war. She then inherited the farm your gel cove in Steneby. However, the real ow
2 CONC ner was her mother, Elin Jacobsdotter Bååt, until about 1646. Mrs. Margareta took 1655 to save the homestead pile to the farmhouse, and the 1656 was recorded both North and south of your gel cove as the pile as her seat yards. She
2 CONC  also owned the Sword village, and from 1664 also Hälgerud. During her lifetime, she gave the children away with their own seating yards. She had 8 children. (Sources: The book "Steneby", the book "Ärtemark-a Dalsland parish" of I
2 CONC  Löfgren)
2 CONT * [https://www.riddarhuset.se/att/svinhufvud-i-westergotland/ '''The genus originates from Dalarna. Elder known ancestor is the mountain man at Stora Kopparberget, Torkil Andersson Tailor (mentioned 1538 and lived in 1551) on Häst
2 CONC berg at Falun.''']  His son, Daniel Tårkilsson, received debt certificate 1581 22/6 at Stockholm's castle by King Johan III with the covenant brought by the family. His first wife, Anna Jönsdotter, was descended from her mother fr
2 CONC om the old medieval Svinhufvudätten in Dalarna.  Her grandson, Major Carl Jönsson Swinehufwudh (dead 1636) to Stora Dingelvik in Steneby parish in Västergötland, which adopted the family name after the coat of arms, was introduced
2 CONC  on behalf of the family 1633 15/2 in the third class, the Swan class, under the current no 199, with the addition in Westergötland after the above-mentioned landscape to the distinction of the other family Svinhufvud. The food wa
2 CONC s moved in 1778 3/11 in the then restored second class, the knights class.  From the end of the 17th century, the main man of the family called himself Qvist and now for Nordqvist. The food is on the women's side feared by the nob
2 CONC le family Svinhufvud of Qvalstad no. 145. The original debt certificate must have been destroyed. 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=4579755&photo_id=6000000190208371839&position=0 '''Medieval stained glass with the boar's head coat of arms in Torsång's church, Dalarna, now in the Historical Museum, 
2 CONC Stockholm. Photo: Riksantikvarieämbetet''']
2 CONT
