1 NAME Håkan /Larsson Svärdsköld/
2 GIVN Håkan
2 SURN Larsson Svärdsköld
2 _MARNM Larsson Svärdsköld
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 DATE 1654
1 DEAT
2 DATE 27 APR 1654
2 PLAC Kvänum, Skaraborgs län, Sverige
2 ADDR
1 OCCU Major, adlad nr 334, Adlad major
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Sv%C3%A4rdsk%C3%B6ld_nr_334
2 CONT
2 CONT Adliga ätten '''SVÄRDSKÖLD''' nr 334 †
2 CONT
2 CONT Adlad 1645-10-06, introd. 1647. Utdöd i början av 1700-talet.
2 CONT
2 CONT I Schlegel & Klingspor, Den ointroducerade adelns ättartavlor, uppgives, att den adlade Håkan Larsson Svärdsköld var broder till Lars Larsson, adlad Silfverswärd, och Jon Larsson, stamfader för adliga ätterna Svärdfelt. Någon anna
2 CONC n källa härför än den svävande uppgiften i Fryxell, Vermlands släktbok, att så skulle hava varit förhållandet, anföres dock icke, och torde heller icke finnas. Vid omnämnandet på riddarhusgenealogien av Lars Silfverswärds änka Cat
2 CONC harina Svenskes omgifte med Håkan Larsson Svärdsköld antydes icke, att de båda männen varit bröder, vilket säkerligen skulle skett, om så varit eller ansetts vara förhållandet. Dessutom skulle k. m:ts tillstånd behövt inhämtas för
2 CONC  Margareta Silfverswärds giftermål med sin styvbroder Lars Svärdsköld, därest de båda kontrahenterna tillika varit kusiner, men något sådant tillstånd synes icke hava påkallats. Håkan Larsson Svärdsköld uppgives haft en dotter Ann
2 CONC a, gift med häradshövdingen Lars Jonsson, adlad Lagerberg, men i personalierna över mannen kallas hon Anna Larsdotter, och hon torde således varit syster till Håkan Larsson. Han hade även en broder, kornetten vid Västgöta ryttare 
2 CONC Bengt Larsson, vilken 1652-12-20 blev adlad med samma namn som brodern, men ej introducerad.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1KA, Reduktionskoll. Akt 139 (OA). TAB 1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Håkan Larsson''', adlad Svärdsköld, till Vistaholm i Floby socken (R), vilket han erhöll i donation 1649-03-29 under Norrköpings besluts villkor, och Nygården i Kvänums socken, som han erhöll genom sitt senare gifte, båda i Ska
2 CONC raborgs län. Ryttmästare vid Västgöta kavalleriregemente. Adlad 1645-10-06 (introd. 1647 under nr 311, vilket nummer sedan ändrats till 334). Major 1650. Död 1654-04-27 och ligger jämte sin andra fru och hennes första man begraven
2 CONC  i Kvänums kyrka. Gift 1:o med N. N. Gift 2:o 1648 med Carin Lennartsdotter Svenske i hennes 2:a gifte (gift 1:o 1629 med överstelöjtnanten Lars Larsson den äldre, adlad Silfverswärd, i hans 2:a gifte, död 1645), död 1678-01-00, d
2 CONC otter av ryttmästaren Lennart Svenske, och Elin Bååt.
2 CONT
2 CONT Barn:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Lars. Förare. Död 1656. Se Tab. 2. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. En son. Stupade under kriget i Polen på 1650-talet. [1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Göran, till Vistaholm, vilket reducerades från honom men utbyttes 1685, samt Brandstorp i Hällestads socken, Älvsborgs län, vilket han en tid innehade genom sitt gifte. Reste 1664 utomlands för att studera krigsväsendet och var
2 CONC  under tio år efter vartannat i holländsk, fransk och italiensk tjänst samt avancerade till major. Levde ännu 1700. Död barnlös och slöt ätten på svärdssidan. 'Han var under sin utländska tjänst sist anställd vid storhertigens av 
2 CONC Toskana garde och kommenderad på galärerna vid Malta. Blev, då den galär, på vilken han tjänstgjorde, sköts i sank av en turkisk kapare, tillfångatagen. Gjorde under fångenskapen Gud ett löfte, till följd varav han efter hemkomste
2 CONC n till fäderneslandet, såväl av det lilla han själv kunnat spara, som av den lilla donation, som hans fader med sitt blod förvärvat, uppbyggde en kyrka samt testamenterade all sin egendom till de fattiga och kyrkobetjäningen, vara
2 CONC  han 1685 anhöll om konfirmation. Gav sedan till kronan 100 punds ränta samt vad han därefter kunde samla.'. Gift 1674 med Märta Krabbe af Svaneby, från vilken han 1693 blev skild, i hennes 2:a gifte (gift 1:o med kaptenen Carl Hå
2 CONC rd af Segerstad, död 1657), död 1699-02-00, dotter av överstelöjtnanten Gustaf Krabbe af Svaneby, och hans 1:a fru Anna Carlsdotter Lilliestielke, nr 120. 
2 CONT
2 CONT TAB 2
2 CONT
2 CONT Lars (son av Håkan Larsson, adlad Svärdsköld, Tab. 1). Förare vid Västgöta kavalleriregemente. Död utan söner 1656 i staden Holland (?) i Preussen. Gift med sin styvsyster Margareta Silfverswärd i hennes 1:a gifte (gift 2:o före 1
2 CONC 660 med sin systers svåger, löjtnanten Göran Dreffensköld, död 1672), död omkr. 1682, dotter av överstelöjtnanten Lars Larsson den äldre, adlad Silfverswärd, och hans 2:a fru Carin Lennartsdotter Svenske.
2 CONT
2 CONT Barn:
2 CONT
2 CONT Agneta, född 1655, död 1712-07-22 på Frändö i Färgelanda socken, Älvsborgs län. Gift före 1684 med majoren Lars Fahnesköld, död omkr. 1702. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Källor:
2 CONT
2 CONT Gustaf Elgenstierna, Den introducerade svenska adelns ättartavlor. 1925-36. 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Tab 1: http://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Sv%C3%A4rdsk%C3%B6ld_nr_334
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT =Major Håkan Larsson, adlad Svärdsköld=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Hakan Larson, Nobll. Srärdskold, to Kullja and: Route master at Wistaholm in Westergöthland Westgotha reg:te; Noble 165%, introd. 1647 under No. 336); Major 1650; + 1654 2; and lies, jemte ein 2nd wife and benne's 1st but buried
2 CONC  in Qramom's church in fürutn. Province. - Married 1:0 with lej known): - 2:0 with Karin Svenske, to Sätra and Altarp, in her 2nd marriage, + 1678; daughter of Ryttmästeren Lennart Pederason Svenske, No. 258, ill Satra, with Elin 
2 CONC Bäat, No. 3, and widow of Ofrerate-Lieutenant Lars Larson, the Elder, Nobil. Silfverswärd, Nso 184, to Wagestorp and Qvänuw
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Sv%C3%A4rdsk%C3%B6ld_nr_334 Noble House Sword Shield No. 334]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Noble House Sword Shield No. 334, Knighted 1645-10-06, introd. 1647. Extinct in the early 18th century.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT In Schlegel & Klingspor, The unintroduced adelns ätartavlor, it is stated that the noble Håkan Larsson Svärdsköld was the brother of Lars Larsson, noble Silfverswärd, and Jon Larsson, progenitor of the noble families Svärdfelt. An
2 CONC y other source for this than the floating information in Fryxell, Vermland's genealogy book, that this would have been the case, is not cited, nor should there be any. In the mention in the knight house genealogy of Lars Silfversw
2 CONC ärd's widow Karin Svenske's remarriage to Håkan Larsson Svärdsköld, it is not implied that the two men were brothers, which would certainly have happened, if that had been or was considered to be the relationship. In addition, the
2 CONC  court's permission had to be obtained for Margareta Silfverswärd's marriage to her stepbrother Lars Svärdsköld, since the two parties were also cousins. but no such condition seems to have been invoked. Håkan 
2 CONT
2 CONT Håkan Larsson , knighted Sword Shield, to Vistaholm in Floby parish, which he received as a donation on 29-03-1649 under the terms of the Norrköping decision, and Nygården in Kvänum parish, which he received through his later marr
2 CONC iage, both in Skaraborg county. Horseman at the Västgöta Cavalry Regiment. Knighted 1645-10-06 (introd. 1647 under no. 311, which number has since been changed to 334). Major 1650. Died 1654-04-27 and is buried with his second wif
2 CONC e and her first husband in Kvänum's church. Married 1st to N . N. [https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000191472031856?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000191488737834 '''Married 2nd in 1648 to Karin Lennartsdotter Svenske in 
2 CONC her 2nd marriage (married 1st in 1629 to lieutenant colonel Lars Larsson the elder, ennobled Silfverswärd , in his 2nd marriage, died 1645), died 1678-01-00, daughter by the master rider Lennart Svenske, and Elin Bååt.''']
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1. '''Lars''' Driver. Died 1656. Lars (son of Håkan Larsson, knighted Sword Shield, Tab. 1). Driver at Västgöta Cavalry Regiment. Died without sons in 1656 in the city of Holland (?) in Prussia. Married to his step-sister Margar
2 CONC eta Silfverswärd in her 1st marriage (married 2nd before 1660 to his sister's brother-in-law, lieutenant Göran Dreffensköld , died 1672), died about 1682, daughter of lieutenant-colonel Lars Larsson the elder, ennobled Silfverswär
2 CONC d , and his 2nd wife Carin Lennartsdotter Swedish . Children: Agneta , born 1655, died 1712-07-22 at Frändö in Färgelanda parish, Älvsborg county. Married before 1684 to Major Lars Fahnesköld , died around 1702.
2 CONT * 1. '''A son.''' Died during the war in Poland in the 1650s. [ 1 ]
2 CONT * 1. '''Goran''', to Vistaholm, which was reduced from him but exchanged in 1685, as well as Brandstorp in Hällestad parish, Älvsborg County, which he held for a time through his marriage. Traveled abroad in 1664 to study the mili
2 CONC tary and was for ten years one after the other in Dutch, French and Italian service and advanced to major. Still alive in 1700. Died childless and ended the family on the side of the sword. 'He was, during his foreign service, las
2 CONC t employed in the guard of the Grand Duke of Tuscany and in charge of the galleys at Malta. When the galley on which he served was shot down by a Turkish privateer, was captured. During the captivity, God made a promise, as a resu
2 CONC lt of which, after returning to his fatherland, both from the little he himself could save, and from the small donation that his father had acquired with his blood, built a church and bequeathed all his property to the poor and th
2 CONC e church service, although he requested confirmation in 1685. Then gave to the Crown £100 interest and what he could afterwards collect.'. Married in 1674 toMärta Krabbe af Svaneby , from whom he was divorced in 1693, in her 2nd m
2 CONC arriage (married 1st to the captain Carl Hård af Segerstad , died 1657), died 1699-02-00, daughter of lieutenant colonel Gustaf Krabbe af Svaneby , and his 1st wife Anna Carlsdotter Lilliestielke .
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Silfversw%C3%A4rd_nr_184 The Noble Family Silfverswärd No. 184]
2 CONT
2 CONT Lars Larssonthe older, adlad Silfverswärd, (son of Lars Jonsson, tab 1), to Badene, which he bought from the Crown 1642-08-30 and Vägestorp and Kvänum, which he received in donation, all in Kvänums parish, Skaraborg County. Was in
2 CONC cluded in the war service circa 1602 and served up from common to rider champion at Västgöta cavalry regiment. Also in charge of the district in Laske, 1624-10-22, which he was still in 1627. Major of the regiment in 1633. Adlad p
2 CONC . 20/10 (intro. 1633 under no. 184). Lieutenant Lieutenant at the same regiment in 1633. Slottshauptman at Älvsborg 1634-10-30. Farewell 1640-08-21. Equestrian at the nobility's rust service in Östergötland, Södermanland, Närke an
2 CONC d Värmland pp. 1/10. Died 1645-08-17 and buried in Kvänum's old, now ruined church. 'He was adored by King Gustaf II Adolf in the camp at Ribnitz in Mecklenburg, however, without any other noble name being allowed to him other tha
2 CONC n that the coat of arms painted on the original letter of honor is signed Larz Larzon Silberschwerdt '. Married 1st with (not known). Married 2nd: 1629, when she received Storebacka in Saleby parish, Skaraborg County in morning gi
2 CONC ft1 , with '''Karin Lydersdotter Svenske in her 1st marriage (married 2nd 1648 to Major Håkan Larsson, adlad Svärdsköld , in his 2nd marriage, died 1654), died 1678-01-00 and lies with both his men and the stepson Olov buried in K
2 CONC vänum according to the inscription on their epitaph, then, daughter of the rider champion Lennart (Linder) Pedersson Svenske and Elin Bååt .'''] According to Palmsköld's Genealogical Collections, Catharina Svenske had three sons w
2 CONC ith Silfverswärd, but in a Swedish family inheritance and payment settlement at the end of the 1600s only the following children Margareta, Agneta and Lars, as her inherited children are included. In March 1648, she was pardoned w
2 CONC ith three homemakers Vånga and Kvänum in the so-called Snr Skaraborg County '.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT *  '''Margareta,''' dead about 1682. Married 1st: with his step brother, driver Lars Svärdsköld , died in 1656. Married 2nd before 1660 with her sister's brother-in-law Lieutenant Göran Dreffensköld , died in 1672.
2 CONT *  '''Agneta,''' dead 1715-03-00 The path and buried s. Å 1/4. Married to Captain Carl Didron , natural. Didron , born 1630, died 1685.
2 CONT * '''Lars,''' the youngest. Cavalry captain. Died 1676. See Tab. 24
2 CONT * '''Maria,''' died in 1691 and buried s. On 4/7 in Gothenburg. Married before 1665 with the rider champion Björn Dreffensköld , died in 1684.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''source''' The noble family Silfverswärd No. 184, Tab 3 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Links=
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://runeberg.org/anrep/4/0317.html
2 CONT
2 CONT =Sources =
2 CONT
2 CONT * EÄ258, Till Säter samt Åttingsåker i Färgelanda sn (P) (1655). Fick Storebacka i Saleby sn (P) i morgongåva av Lars Silfverswärd.  Ligger jämte båda sina män och styvsonen Olov begr i Kvänum enligt påskriften å deras epitafium d
2 CONC ärst. "Catarina Svenske skulle enligt Palmskölds Genalogiska samlingar haft med Silfverswärd tre söner, men uti en Svenske-ättens arvs- och vederlagslikvid i slutet av 1600-talet upptages då endast de nedanstående barnen    Margar
2 CONC eta, Agneta och Lars, såsom hennes i arv delaktiga barn; hon blev 1648-03-20 benådad med tre hemman Vånga och Kvänum i likan.  snr (Skar)."    
2 CONT * KA, Reduction check. Act 139 (OA).
2 CONT * Gustaf Elgenstierna , The introduced genealogical tables of the Swedish nobility. 1925-36.
