1 NAME Catharine /Murray/
2 GIVN Catharine
2 SURN Murray
2 _MARNM Murray
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1586
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1669
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} MAURITZDOTTER, CATHARINA [SSNE 6255]
2 CONT
2 CONT Surname
2 CONT     MAURITZDOTTER, MURRAY, MAURITZ, THOMSON First name
2 CONT     CATHARINA Nationality
2 CONT     SCOT
2 CONT
2 CONT Text
2 CONT
2 CONT Catharina Mauritzdotter Murray [1586-1669] was the wife of Thomas Thomson [SSNE 1648]. They had 15 children, many of whom were also in Swedish military service, most prominently Patrick [SSNE 3670] and Alexander [SSNE 3664]. Catha
2 CONC rina became a widow in 1643. On 10 July 1645 she received confirmation of of the estates of Vrana and Munkevrak. She is mentioned in correspondence by her son Alexander's heirs.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources: Riksarkivets ämnessamlingar. Personhistoria https://sok.riksarkivet.se/bildvisning/A0074122_00137#?c=&m=&s=&cv=136&xywh=2584%2C2292%2C4019%2C2203
2 CONT
2 CONT https://sok.riksarkivet.se/bildvisning/A0074122_00207#?c=&m=&s=&cv=206&xywh=2478%2C2452%2C3349%2C1836
2 CONT
2 CONT Svenska Adelns Ättartavlor, vol. 8, pp.264-265; F. Fryxell, Wermelandia Nobilitata, list compiled at Landsarkivet Göteborg, (1945) p.31; H. Marryat, One Year in Sweden, including a visit to the isle of Gotland (London, 1862), p.49
2 CONC 9.
2 CONT
2 CONT Two letters from 'Catharina Mauritz' were sent to Axel Oxenstierna. One is dated 1636, the other is undated. See SRA, Oxenstiernska samlingen E740. Catharina Moritz to Axel Oxenstierna, 1x December 1636 and 1x undated.
2 CONT
2 CONT Female. Service record
2 CONT
2 CONT SWEDEN,
2 CONT     Arrived 1586-01-01
2 CONT     Departed 1669-12-31
2 CONT     Purpose MISC.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.st-andrews.ac.uk/history/ssne/item.php?id=6255
2 CONT -------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Catherine Murray, a correspondent of the Swedish Chancellor and Regent, Axel Oxenstierna, long before the death of her husband, Colonel Thomas Thomson, also received confirmation of her land in Vrana and Munkevrak after his death,
2 CONC  doubtless due to the chancellor’s mediation.
2 CONT
2 CONT Den introducerade Svenska Adelns Ättartavlor vol. 8, 264-265. See also Murdoch and Grosjean 2014, 249. For her previous correspondence with Oxenstierna, see RA/OS, E740. ʻCatharina Moritz’ to Axel Oxenstierna, December 1636 and an
2 CONC other ʻundated’.
