1 NOTE {geni:about_me} THOMSON, ESKIL [SSNE 3666]
2 CONT
2 CONT Surname
2 CONT     THOMSON First name
2 CONT     ESKIL Title/rank
2 CONT     CAPTAIN Nationality
2 CONT     SCOT Social status
2 CONT     NOBILITY
2 CONT
2 CONT Text source
2 CONT
2 CONT Eskil Thomson was the son of Thomas Thomson and Catherine Murray. He served as an ensign with Alexander Leslie's Narke och Varmland regiment in 1622. He became a lieutenant in 1626 but was reformed in 1631. Thomson was promoted ca
2 CONC ptain in 1633 and a commander for a company in Wurzburg garrison. He was later a captain of Skaraborg's regiment in 1635 in which capacity he still served when the garrison was stationed in Wismar in 1639. He probably died in Febr
2 CONC uary 1643.
2 CONT
2 CONT Stockholm Krigsarkivet, Muster Roll, 1622/4; 1623/3; 1626/1,8,10; 1627/12; 1629/3,8,10; 1631/4; 1633/6,8; 1635/1,9,14; 1636/1,11,22; 1637/3,10; 1638/4,9,12,24; 1639/4,7; 1640/7; 1641/8,17-25; 1642/7; 1643/9. Svenska Adelns Attarta
2 CONC vlor, vol. 8, p.265; C.O. Nordensvan, (ed.), Värmlands Regementes [Närkes och Värmlands Regementes] Historia: Andra Delen, Personal Historia (Stockholm, 1911), p.28. Service record
2 CONT
