1 NOTE {geni:about_me} THOMSON, SAMUEL [SSNE 3674]
2 CONT
2 CONT Surname
2 CONT     THOMSON First name
2 CONT     SAMUEL Title/rank
2 CONT     COLONEL? Nationality
2 CONT     SCOT Social status
2 CONT     OFFICER
2 CONT
2 CONT Text source
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel Thomson was the son of Thomas Thomason and Catherine Murray. He served first as captain in Konrad Techelborg's Sodermanland, Narke and Varmland regiment in 1622. He was apointed colonel quartermaster with Alexander Leslie's
2 CONC  Sodermanlanm, Narke and Varmland regiment in 1623. There he became a major in 1626 and a lieutenant captain in 1629 when the regiment was taken over by John Kinnemond. He served in his father's company in 1633 and is said in some
2 CONC  sources to  have died in 1634/1635 (Nordensvan). However a man of the same name appears on the muster-rolls long after, reaching the rank of [lt?] colonel.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Stockholm Krigsarkivet, Muster Roll, 1622/2,4; 1623/3; 1626/7,8,10; 1627/11-13; 1628/7; 1629/3,8,10; 1631/4; 1633/6; 1634/2,5,18-23; 1635/1,9,20-25,27,31,32. NB 1636/1,15,17-19; 1637/3,7,15,16; 1638/4,5,9,21,24-27; 1638/4 DEAD; S
2 CONC venska Adelns Attartavlor, vol. 8, p.265; C.O. Nordensvan, (ed.), Värmlands Regementes [Närkes och Värmlands Regementes] Historia: Andra Delen, Personal Historia (Stockholm, 1911), p.38.
2 CONT
2 CONT The second Samuel Thomson is noted in MR 1639/1,4,13-17; 1640/2,4; 1641/2,5; 1642/2,4,19-21; 1643/2,3,5 Service record
2 CONT
