2 CONT '''Svarte Ture Jönsson also called "Thure Swarte Jonsson" and "Thure Jonsson Swarte".''' Said to be 50 years old in 1477, although he is mentioned in letters before the 60-year-old brother Åke in 1477. Appears at the earliest in 1
2 CONC 440 and then without a knighthood, but had one on 1.2 1442, which is why he must have been dubbed at the coronation of King Kristofer on 14.9 1441. Mentioned as a councilor from 1453 and as a lawman in Västergötland from 1454 and 
2 CONC again in 1480. In 1457 he became a chieftain at Ax vall, where he 1462 was succeeded by his brother Åke. Still alive 10.2 1481 and died 28.4 the same year and was buried in Vadstena. Married at the latest in 1455 to Birgitta Henri
2 CONC ksdotter, who was still alive in 1500 and was the daughter of the Riksdag Henrik Snakenborg , whose wife's name is not known.
