2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Arvid Jönsson.'''Circuit Judge. 
2 CONT
2 CONT =1625 introduced the Great Store,=
2 CONT
2 CONT Together riddarhusgenealogien under the name Store, both the so-called blue or Aspenäs dynasty, which utdog in the mid 1400s and the Force conducted a so-called lejonörn, and Jöns Bengtssons lineage (see below), whose coat of arms
2 CONC  image from Jöns Bengtssons Son Arvid Jönsson (Tab. 2), it was the genealogies called "Storevapnet": a Sparre over a star, which was also taken by the Great Great at the time of the introduction. In reality, however, there is no c
2 CONC onnection between the Blue Eight and the other two eats, and even the relationship between the two latter eighteons assumed in riddarhus genealogy is highly doubtful. By Jöns Bengtsson, one member, Olof Arvidsson, took up his moth
2 CONC er's weapon, half a punch over a chess box, and became an ancestor of the Countess Stenbock, While another member, Olof Nilsson (Tab. 7), took up his surname Drake, but retained the fathers' weapon (Sparre over a star) and became 
2 CONC ancestor of the united widow Drake of Intorp.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jöns Bengtsson , born in the 1340s. Bought a farm in Redslarp (now Betstorp) in Gällstads parish, Kinds härad (page 151), Älvsborgs län 1385-09-23. Heardshövding i Kind 1397-06-09 and yet (Sd.) 1409-09-09. Cited resident in Kind (
2 CONC Sd.) 1412-05-26. Bring a sparrow to the gun.
2 CONT
