0 @N6000000006127719178@ NOTE A soldier by the name of Anders Bengtsson, fell in action in the service of Gustavus Adolphus, married Kerstin Bengtsdotter and had issue a son, Lars Fegier, born 1601 at Saleby parish, ennobled with the surname Fegierskiöld which
1 CONC  was changed toFägerskiöld, killed in action 5 February 1659 at the siege of Hald (now Fredrikshall), Norway, buried 8 May 1659 at Trässberg church, Sweden, married 1640 Margareta Rutensköld (died 1652). Other than the below menti
1 CONC oned, one son and two daughtersdied young. Their surviving issue was:1. Lars Fägerskiöld, died 5 March 1683, buried Åsaka church, married Anna Lennartsdotter Lake (buried 16 May 1711 at Vinköl church).2. Maria, died after 1676, ma
1 CONC rried before 1666 Sven Grotte (died 1675).3. Christian Fägerskiöld, killed in action 4 December 1676 at the battle of Lund, buried Åsaka church.4. baron Fromhold Fägerskiöld, died 20 October 1706, buried 15 November 1706 at Örebro
1 CONC  church, married Catharina Lillie af Aspenäs.
